  "body": "**What happens:** on `upstream/main` d251029, which includes #447, the v0.15.0 release, three UI pixel goldens fail:\n\n```\negui_app::tests::egui_shell_snapshot        'egui_app'          Diff: 23\negui_app::tests::egui_shell_snapshot_light  'egui_app_light'    Diff: 23\negui_app::tests::tool_editor_snapshot       'egui_tool_editor'  Diff: 23\n```\n\nRun with `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib -- egui_shell_snapshot tool_editor_snapshot` from `crates/ui` (macOS, debug).\n\n- All three show the same small diff (23) in the same region. That points at the ribbon's build-identity label (#352): the version text changed from v0.14.0 to v0.15.0 at the cut, and the goldens still show the old version.\n- The three passed before the release merge. Every open PR gate now shows them red.\n\n**Suggested fix:**\n- Either re-render the three goldens on the platform they were made on, after the version bump. That makes it a release-step chore: re-render the goldens after `release.ps1` bumps the version.\n- Or have the snapshot harness pin the build-identity label to a fixed test string, the way the timestamp is already \"01-01 00:00 UTC\", so a version bump never changes a golden.\n\nThe second option removes the problem for every future cut. #255 / PR #359 (snapshots out of the PR flow) is related, but #359 is still open.\n\nThe contributor didn't re-render on macOS, because the goldens' platform anti-aliasing differs (#255).\n\n**Done means:** the three tests pass on main, and a version bump no longer breaks them.\n",
